# CLASS-BY-NAME FACTORY (`_N("<Class>")(<kwargs>)`) — WORKING PARTIAL BUILD, banked 2026-08-27.
#
# APPLY WITH:  git apply getting-better/pyast-expr/class-by-name-factory-WIP.patch
#
# This is the capability the pure_ast census named as gating 73 of the 96 trusted `_Parser`
# stubs (12% of the whole TCB). It is REVERTED out of the tree per demand-first discipline —
# every piece below is measured BYTE-INERT (mirror emission diff 0 of 52, corpus 0 of 813) but
# has NO CONSUMER yet, and an unconsumed capability is surface without value. It is banked
# verbatim so the next window re-derives NOTHING.
#
# EXACTLY HOW FAR IT GETS, measured on `_Parser._import_as_name` (the best consumer: it RETURNS
# the construction directly instead of funnelling it through the trusted `_fin`):
#
#   before:  return _N("alias")(name=name, asname=asname)   emitted as   0
#   after :  { py_alias_name = !name;
#              py_alias_asname = (match !asname with Arm_2_0 _v -> _v | _ -> "" end) }
#
# i.e. the record is declared, the return type is `py_alias`, the constructor binds BOTH real
# arguments, and the `Optional[str]` local really does become a union carrier.
#
# THE FOUR PIECES, each independently useful:
#  1. Module5_IREmitter `_py_expr_call` — resolve `<Name>("<lit>")(<kwargs>)` to a direct
#     `<lit>(…)` Call. `pure_ast._N(name)` is `_g[name]` over the namespace `_build_nodes`
#     fills from `_NODE_SPEC`, so at a literal site the class is STATICALLY KNOWN; resolving
#     it reuses the whole existing record-construction path (WL-07 keyword binding included).
#  2. ir_resolve `_resolve_same_file_node_spec_records` — the SAME-FILE `_NODE_SPEC` harvest.
#     `_harvest_node_spec_records` was only ever called for a DEPENDENCY, so when `pure_ast.py`
#     itself is under verification its own ASDL table was never harvested. Injects a record
#     only when a PARAM or RETURN annotation names it (bare or quoted).
#  3. ir_resolve `_harvest_node_spec_records` — synthesize `init_params`/`init_body` for a
#     harvested record. `_build_nodes` gives every node class the shared `AST.__init__`, which
#     binds positional args to `cls._fields` in order and keywords BY NAME (pure_ast.py:111),
#     so "params = field names, body = field f := param f" is an EXACT model. WITHOUT IT the
#     WL-07 keyword binding has nothing to bind through and every construction collapses to
#     its all-defaults witness.
#  4. preamble — `use option.Option` when a harvested RECORD carries an `option`-typed FIELD
#     (`alias.asname`). Measured: `unbound type symbol 'option'` on the record decl line.
#  (+ the `"OptStr"` field tag, the string twin of `"OptExprIR"`, and the `alias` table entry.)
#
# THE ONE REMAINING BLOCKER, precisely located:
#   `let asname = ref ""` — the union local is DECLARED `string` instead of
#   `(Arm_2_None : _union__import_as_name_2)`. `statements.py:4178` builds `_union_locals` from
#   `_current_symbol_table[name].startswith("_union_")`, and the ANNOTATED-LOCAL path
#   (`asname: Optional[str] = None`, runtime-inert under PEP 526) creates the union ARMS but
#   never writes the symbol-table entry. Fix that seeding and `_import_as_name` converts.
#   Second, smaller: the option-typed FIELD WRITE unwraps the union to a bare string
#   (`| _ -> ""`) instead of building `None`/`Some` — faithful only once the field write knows
#   the target is `option string`.
#
# ALSO NOTE, from the same census: almost every OTHER `_N` construction in `_Parser` is wrapped
# in `self._fin(_N(...)(...), t)`, and `_fin` SETS FOUR LOCATION ATTRIBUTES on a node whose type
# varies per call site. So `_fin` — not `_N` — is the gate for the remaining ~71 stubs, and it
# is a distinct (harder) capability: per-node field WRITES through an untyped parameter.
#
